  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Go to homepage M\u00f8lle \u00ae Overview Buy M\u00f8lle Skog Studio, 24 m\u00b2 \u20ac68,000 Sj\u00f6 One bedroom, 48 m\u00b2 \u20ac124,000 Lia Two storey, 86 m\u00b2 \u20ac186,000 Kust Twin gable, 132 m\u00b2 \u20ac248,000 All homes Overview Buy M\u00f8lle Close Homes How it works Pricing Configure Visit a cabin More Add-ons Customers About Journal Talk to us Enquire Contact [email protected] Our cabins Four prefab cabins, built indoors and delivered finished to your plot. Skog Studio, 24 m\u00b2 \u20ac68,000 Sj\u00f6 One bedroom, 48 m\u00b2 \u20ac124,000 Lia Two storey, 86 m\u00b2 \u20ac186,000 Kust Twin gable, 132 m\u00b2 \u20ac248,000 Questions we hear a lot Anything else, ask the studio nearest to you. Contact a studio How long does the whole process take? Four to six months from the first call to the keys. Permits take the most time; the cabin itself is built in ten to fourteen weeks. Can I change the layout or the finishes? Within each model, yes. You choose the kitchen, the floors, the stove and the window positions on the long walls. The cladding comes in tarred pine, natural larch or silvered larch. Only the shape stays the same. Who prepares the plot? Our local crews do. They lay the foundation, bring in water and power, and leave the plot ready for crane day. I",
